tands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le01ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Describing Cities"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use adjectives to describe cities.<br/><br/>Here are some adjectives and their opposites."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Recife was very modern and exciting, but very busy. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "It's beautiful."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":11,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjective\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Opposite\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"modern\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" old, ancient, historic\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"beautiful\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"ugly\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"calm\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"busy, crowded\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"quiet\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"loud, noisy\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"pleasant\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"unpleasant\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"cheap\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" expensive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"clean\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"polluted\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"hot, warm\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" cold, cool\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"large\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"small\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"exciting\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"boring\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Expressing Disbelief"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Disbelief means you don't believe something, or you have a hard time believing something. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: I got a bad sunburn even though I wore sunblock.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: That's incredible!"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You express disbelief using expressions. These expressions are often used as a polite way to keep the conversation going.<br/><br/>Often, you don't really mean you do not believe the person. You mean what they are saying is uncommon, strange or unusual.<br/><br/>No way!<br/>You don't say!<br/>That is incredible!<br/>It's unbelievable!<br/>I can't believe it!<br/>I can't imagine!"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to refer"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be associated with "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The name refers to the stone reefs around the city. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le01ob07aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about a new city."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "incredible"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "amazing; great"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The city of Recife was incredible. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le01ob07aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "university"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an institution for advanced education"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are many important universities and hospitals."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le01ob07aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "wore"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the verb to wear in the Simple Past tense"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I got a bad sunburn even though I wore sunblock."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le01ob07aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "World Heritage Site"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an official designation of the United Nations as a place that is very important for history"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The town of Olinda is a World Heritage Site because of the colonial architecture."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le01ob07aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pleasant"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "agreeable; nice to be in "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Olinda is a small, pleasant town."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le01ob07aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write a list of 5 cities in the world."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Choose 3 adjectives that describe each city. Write the adjectives on a separate paper."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ask your partner to guess which city goes with which adjectives."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss what you know about the cities."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Change roles. Ask your partner to think of 5 different cities."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I choose 5 cities."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I describe the cities."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I play the guessing game with a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I discuss the cities."}]}], "type": "sena"}